direction: down

title: |md
  ## Argument access by program type
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

fentry: "fentry/fexit" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("fentry/vfs_read")
    int BPF_PROG(p,
      struct file *f, char *buf,
      size_t n, loff_t *pos)
    { ... }
    ```
    **Does:**
    - trampoline supplies BTF-typed function args

    **State:**
    - `f` is trusted `PTR_TO_BTF_ID`
    - direct field reads are allowed
  |
}

kprobe: "kprobe/kretprobe" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("kprobe/vfs_read")
    int BPF_KPROBE(p,
      struct file *f, ...) { ... }
    ```
    **Does:**
    - trap saves CPU registers in `struct pt_regs`

    **State:**
    - extracted pointers are scalars
    - use `bpf_probe_read_kernel` for fields
  |
}

tracepoint: "tracepoint/..." {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("tracepoint/syscalls/
      sys_enter_read")
    int p(struct
      trace_event_raw_sys_enter
      *ctx)
    ```
    **Does:**
    - reads a copied event struct

    **State:**
    - stable fields from `events/.../format`
    - under `/sys/kernel/tracing/`
    - not live kernel objects
  |
}

rawtp: "raw_tracepoint/..." {
  style.fill: "#fde68a"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("raw_tracepoint/sched_switch")
    int p(struct
      bpf_raw_tracepoint_args *ctx)
    ```
    **Does:**
    - exposes raw tracepoint args
    - as positional `u64` slots

    **State:**
    - lower-level than tracepoint
    - caller must unpack by index
  |
}

tpbtf: "tp_btf/..." {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  body: |md
    ```c
    SEC("tp_btf/sched_switch")
    int BPF_PROG(p, bool preempt,
      struct task_struct *prev,
      struct task_struct *next)
    ```
    **Does:**
    - uses tracepoint BTF prototype

    **State:**
    - live typed pointers
    - for the whole callback
  |
}

fentry -> kprobe
kprobe -> tracepoint
tracepoint -> rawtp
rawtp -> tpbtf

legend: |md
  **Why move down the chain**
  - fentry -> kprobe:
  - older trap path, same target
  - kprobe -> tracepoint:
  - explicit events avoid fragile fn names
  - tracepoint -> raw_tracepoint:
  - skip copied struct when raw args wanted
  - raw_tracepoint -> tp_btf:
  - BTF restores typed arguments
| {near: bottom-center; shape: text}
